Review written to `docs/reviews/solar-deep/solar-deep-05-omni-azimuth-integration.md`.

**Summary of findings:**

- **1 high** — Docstring at `solar.rs:319` falsely claims 0.5% convergence; measured error is ~2.3% for N=12 on vertical walls
- **2 medium** — Integration error scales with tilt (worst at 90°); worst-case irradiance error reaches ~9 W/m² for vertical surfaces at high zenith
- **2 low** — Existing tests correctly use 5% tolerance (consistent with actual error); HARES is unique among compared codes in performing azimuth integration for diffuse sky

The root cause is that N=12 samples of a smooth periodic function produces O(1/N²) convergence, yielding ~2.3% error on the analytical integral. N=30+ is required for the claimed <0.5% accuracy.
